# STACKIT Landing Zone Accelerator: **${platform_identifier}**

%{ if playground_mode ~}
> **Playground mode.** The platform identifier carries a random suffix so this deployment does not
> occupy a name for good. Publish this platform or the STACKIT Project definition to other
> workspaces only to test that path, and delete the playground afterwards.

%{ endif ~}
| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Organization** | [Open in STACKIT Portal](${organization_url}) (`${organization_id}`) |
| **Root Folder** | [Open in STACKIT Portal](${root_folder_url}) (`${root_folder_name}`, `${root_folder_id}`) |
| **Management Project** | [Open in STACKIT Portal](${management_project_url}) (`${management_project_id}`) |
| **STACKIT Project Service Account** | `${service_account_email}` |

## Network Areas

%{ if length(network_areas) == 0 ~}
The export has no connectivity, so the run created no network area.
%{ else ~}
The run created the hub and spoke networking of the export.
[Open the network areas in STACKIT Portal](${network_areas_url})

| Area | Network Area ID |
|------|-----------------|
%{ for area, id in network_areas ~}
| `${area}` | `${id}` |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ endif ~}

## Landing Zones

%{ if length(landing_zones) == 0 ~}
The export has no landing zones, so the platform has none either.
%{ else ~}
| Landing Zone | Folder |
|--------------|--------|
%{ for name, folder in landing_zones ~}
| `${name}` | `${folder}` |
%{ endfor ~}
%{ endif ~}

Application teams add **STACKIT Project** from the marketplace to a tenant on one of these landing
zones. The project is created in the landing zone's folder.
